Project Implementation Phase

1. Introduction

The Project Implementation Phase involves converting the project design into a working application using suitable programming languages and development tools.

2. Objectives

- Develop the project based on the approved design.
- Implement the required features and modules.
- Integrate all modules into a complete system.
- Identify and fix coding errors.
- Ensure the application works as expected.

3. Development Process

The project is developed step by step using the selected programming languages, frameworks, and tools.

4. Module Development

Each module is implemented separately to make development and debugging easier.

5. System Integration

All developed modules are combined to create a complete working application.

6. Error Handling

Errors are identified, debugged, and corrected to improve application reliability.

7. Expected Outcome

A working application developed according to the project requirements and design.

8. Conclusion

The Project Implementation Phase transforms the planned design into a functional system ready for testing.
